## Compiled Binary License Notice

The compiled firmware binaries (`.ino.bin` files in `firmware/`) are subject to
the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later), because
they incorporate ESP8266Audio 2.4.1 (Copyright (c) 2016-2024 Earle F. Philhower, III),
which is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later. ESP8266Audio in turn embeds libmad
(Copyright (c) 2000-2004 Underbit Technologies, Inc.), licensed GPL-2.0-or-later.

The full text of the GNU General Public License version 3 is in
`LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt`.

ESP8266Audio source: https://github.com/earlephilhower/ESP8266Audio (version 2.4.1)

Corresponding Source for the compiled binaries includes:
- The author's source files in this repository (`.ino`, `.h`)
- ESP8266Audio 2.4.1 source code, included in `third-party/ESP8266Audio-2.4.1/`
  (libmad included; original license and copyright notices preserved)
- Build instructions in README.md (section: ビルド in 対応環境（技術的な事項）)

The ESP8266Audio source bundled in `third-party/ESP8266Audio-2.4.1/` is provided
for GPL Corresponding Source compliance. It is a verbatim copy of ESP8266Audio 2.4.1
as installed from https://github.com/earlephilhower/ESP8266Audio. Building the
firmware uses the system-installed library, not the bundled copy.
